description.narrative:
Output: Output 1
Original project: National targeting system to select poor households implemented efficiently
Overall project: [unchanged] 
Indicator: By 2019 (nationwide): At least 25 national programs use the Listahanan targeting
mechanism 
Achievement: 15 
Progress/Status: As of April 2017, original target was exceeded  with 22 national programs utilizing Listahanan 1 (target under original project was 3 national programs). During process of the additional financing, target was increased to 25.  

Currently, there are 15 NGAs that use the Listahanan 2 database: 


1. Complementation to the Municipal Fisherfolk Registry to identify poor farmers (Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources );
2. Convergence on Livelihood Assistance for ARBs Project (CLAAP- DAR)
3. Universal Health Care for indigent clients (PHILHEALTH);
4. Unconditional Cash Transfer Program (DOF- TRAIN);
5. Milk Supplementation Program (Phil. Carabao Center);
6. Unified Financial Assistance System for Tertiary Education Act (UniFAST - CHED);
7. NFA Discounted Rice Subsidy (National Food Authority);
8. Social Pension Program (DSWD);
9. Sustainable Livelihood Program (DSWD);
10. Regular Pantawid Pamilya Program (DSWD);
11. Modified Conditional Cash Transfer (MCCT - DSWD)
12. For updating the base map used for the Predictive Analysis for Humanitarian Response (PAHR) tool - DREAMB
13. Prioritization of IPs in poverty programs (NCIP);
14. Identification of indigent families in identified municipalities for livelihood programs (OPAPP);
15. Implementing poverty reduction through rural development program (NAPC)

The databased is also used for research, planning, evaluation & enhancement of government programs. 
Data Source: Database of NHTS-PR (DSWD); Impact evaluation of the 4Ps (DSWD); NHTS-PR annual report (DSWD)
